{"id": "EUVD-2026-82027", "enisaUuid": "b388fdee-d1c8-30f8-93bd-2e208aac0e69", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: reserve space for the CSA-abort countdown TLV\n\nWhen a CSA countdown is active, mt7996_mcu_beacon_cntdwn() emits two\nbss_bcn_cntdwn_tlv entries (the CSA countdown and the CCA-abort BCC), but\nMT7996_BEACON_UPDATE_SIZE only reserved one. With MBSSID enabled and a\nnear-maximum beacon template the extra 8 bytes could push the offload\ncommand past MT7996_MAX_BSS_OFFLOAD_SIZE and trigger skb_over_panic().\nReserve room for both countdown TLVs.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:25", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d348f96623ec20d700af7d4dfc00a74da6238ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc1d694a1ffe0062c3adf0db1d64ad54454398ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45d8896e4cffffb2c6554ccbec6efe7a0d53166f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a51aff0e048dc5b8252d65808b79939c942d6ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50c66bab321140c49aa2ed779a3ec9d2f085b458"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90366", "GHSA-9rj4-wjx5-8xc6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "055a0929-5553-382f-8459-a3bc1f956630", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "08aa4148-d5dc-3252-bf61-54f1cabe7a0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98686cd21624c75a043e96812beadddf4f6f48e5 <bc1d694a1ffe0062c3adf0db1d64ad54454398ec"}, {"id": "163e0eaf-0cf1-304c-b504-9af64be6735b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "5473a8b3-ef05-38a2-9662-bd3e1dbca860", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98686cd21624c75a043e96812beadddf4f6f48e5 <45d8896e4cffffb2c6554ccbec6efe7a0d53166f"}, {"id": "6a247685-0b41-3aef-bdbb-ed1a03f807ce", "product"